{"body":"Plan B of the issue-watcher claim handoff (Decision 6 = B), run through /sc:implement on top of Plan A (#584) and the recorded first live test.\n\n## What it changes\n1. `WORKER-CONTRACT.md` gains the coordinator's \"Issue pipeline duties\", the worker's plan-approval rule WC-17 and a `path:<existing worktree>` brief slot.\n2. The watcher now claims with `--pipeline none`; the `sc:issue` command, skill and claim ref carry one coordinator-handoff paragraph in the same words.\n3. Launch-level guard G2: a bound worker may run `orchestration send` and `ask` only to its own coordinator (no `--to`, or `--to run:<id>`). Also a `release-worker` helper, an `orca_worktree.py pending` subcommand and an optional launch marker line in the worker brief. The guard is a security hook; the plugin copy is byte-identical.\n4. Design note `docs/designs/issue-pipeline-guard-g2.md`, and the watcher design, setup runbook and technical reference amended for the handoff.\n\n## Merge order warning\nThe watcher prompt switch (`--pipeline none`) must not merge before a running coordinator carries the Task 9 duties: after it, no agent starts for a claimed issue until the coordinator starts a worker. The guard change needs its own independent review before merge.\n\n## Tests\n- `uv run pytest tests/hooks/ -k launch_level`: 4265 passed, 13 skipped\n- the Task 15 command: 4554 passed, 13 skipped\n- `make verify-sync`: clean\n\n## Known follow-ups\n- Two stale sentences: `docs/designs/issue-watcher.md` line 15 and row A1b of the technical reference.\n- The coordinator duties do not yet name the `release-worker` step.\n- The G2 note lists four facts still to measure (for example how the coordinator reads a worker's session id).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n","files":[{"path":".dev/tasks/done/TASK-WF-planDecision6BFo-20261114-174909/TASK-WF-planDecision6BFo-20261114-174909.md","additions":234,"deletions":0,"changeType":"ADDED"},{"path":".dev/tasks/done/T